      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 300 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Bamboo slips buried in a tomb at Guodian preserve the oldest known passages of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daodejing">Daodejing</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">142</span><span class="rf-text">Zhang Daoling receives a revelation from the deified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laozi">Laozi</a> and founds the Way of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/way-of-the-five-pecks-of-rice">Celestial Masters</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">184</span><span class="rf-text">The Yellow Turban rebellion of the Way of Great Peace shakes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">442</span><span class="rf-text">The Northern Wei emperor Taiwu receives Daoist registers, making Daoism the religion of his state</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">666</span><span class="rf-text">The Tang emperor Gaozong honours <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laozi">Laozi</a>, the dynasty’s claimed ancestor, as an emperor</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1167</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-chongyang">Wang Chongyang</a> founds the monastic school of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quanzhen-school">Complete Perfection</a> (Quanzhen)</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1222</span><span class="rf-text">The Quanzhen master Qiu Chuji meets <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-kush">Hindu Kush</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1445</span><span class="rf-text">The Ming court completes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> of the Daoist Canon</span></li></ol>
